    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "Both tests pass and the full build succeeds. Here's a summary of the change.\n\n## Soft-delete for owners\n\nThe requirement was to make `DELETE /api/owners/{id}` a soft-delete: flag the owner `deleted` and keep the row, keep it readable via GET, default `deleted` to false on create, and have the create endpoint's duplicate/identity checks ignore deleted owners.\n\n**Changes, each in the layer where it belongs:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a persisted `deleted` boolean column with `isDeleted()`/`setDeleted()`. This is the single source of truth for the flag.\n\n2. **DB schemas** (`db/{hsqldb,h2,postgres,mysql}/schema.sql`) \u2014 added a `deleted BOOLEAN DEFAULT FALSE NOT NULL` column. The tests run under `hsqldb` with `ddl-auto=none`, so the column must exist in the schema script; a fresh insert defaults it to false.\n\n3. **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` property to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries the field and MapStruct maps it automatically. This is what surfaces `$.deleted` in the GET/create responses.\n\n4. **`service/ClinicServiceImpl.deleteOwner`** \u2014 changed from `ownerRepository.delete(owner)` to `owner.setDeleted(true); ownerRepository.save(owner)`, so the delete flow marks and retains the record (returning the existing 204, which is 2xx).\n\n5. **Duplicate/identity checks ignore deleted owners** \u2014 added a `!isDeleted()` filter to `ClinicServiceImpl.isHouseholdDuplicate` (the blocking identity check) and to `PossibleDuplicateDetector` (the soft-duplicate signal). Since deleted owners never exist in the other tests, this is a no-op there and only relaxes a block once the sole match has been soft-deleted.\n\nI kept the change scoped to the duplicate/identity detection the spec calls out, reusing the existing `isDeleted()` predicate rather than duplicating filtering logic. Test result: `Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` \u2014 `coreSoftDeleteFlagsAndRetains` and `coreDeletedOwnerIgnoredByDuplicateCheck` both green.",
